# A path is ignored only if it is (a) a size constraint, (b) machine-generated
# and regenerated automatically, or (c) a credential. Everything the agent
# needs in order to RUN is tracked, so `git archive HEAD` produces a complete,
# portable copy of the agent for another Databricks workspace.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because the zip must stay functional:
#   app/frontend/dist/  - the workspace serves it; there is no build step there
#   standards/*.docx + standards/*.json, templates/*, *.xlsx
#                       - config and templates the agent reads at run time

# (a) size
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# (b) machine-generated. .databricks/ is the Databricks CLI's local state: it
# pins THIS workspace's job id and user paths, so it must never travel to
# another workspace. `databricks bundle deploy` rebuilds it from databricks.yml.
.databricks/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
src/*.egg-info/

# (c) credentials. The README's `cp .env.example .env` creates a real one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# runtime output
local_data/

# OS / editor junk
.DS_Store
~$*
.~lock.*#
